[quote][b]I'm working on all of these mods on my own.[/b] If you'd like to help, extend or fix one of them, co-author a new one, or join one of my bigger projects, I'm very open to it. Send me a message here on Nexus or on the [b]FarCry:Modding Discord Server[/b].[/quote]

Realistic damage and enemy shooting. A bullet that connects is serious for you and for a mercenary, and whether it connects depends on range, movement, how well the shooter sees you, recoil and the time he needs to settle his aim. Hard, but every death has a reason you can read.

[b][size=4]What it changes[/size][/b]
[list]
[*][b]Real rounds[/b] - every gun hits as hard as its real cartridge, whoever fires it: one torso hit from a rifle drops a soldier, two from a pistol, a head hit from anything kills. A soldier's gun hurts you as much as yours hurts him, and no gun gains damage up close.[/*]
[*][b]Blood only from buckshot[/b] - a bullet that hits you or a soldier no longer throws a spray of blood; a shotgun's pellets still do.[/*]
[*][b]Difficulty is how much you can take[/b] - from full health an AK-47 hit kills you on Infamous, the third on Hardcore, the fifth on Normal and about the eighth on Easy, wherever it lands; the soldiers aim and hit the same on every setting. On Easy and Normal your last bar still softens hits, as in the game, and on Hardcore and Infamous no longer does.[/*]
[*][b]Wounds heal on their own[/b] - above your last bar health climbs back to full: on Easy from half a second after the last hit, in 2 seconds; on Normal from 2 seconds, in 4 seconds; on Hardcore from 5 seconds, in 5 minutes; never on Infamous. The game refilled only the bar you were in. On your last bar you still bleed and need the surgery, as in the game.[/*]
[*][b]Limb hits wound[/b] - a hit to an arm or a leg that would kill a soldier puts him down wounded instead: he calls for help, crawls for cover and may shoot back from the ground. A torso hit never does: it wounds or kills.[/*]
[*][b]Aim is earned[/b] - a soldier who spots you up close fires at once; farther out he takes longer to make up his mind, 3 seconds at 50 m, and his aim settles meanwhile. Every shot is a real chance and none is certain, recoil spoils his follow-up shots, and you are harder to hit running across his line of fire than running at him. He never aims at your head in his first 3 seconds on you.[/*]
[*][b]Fire discipline[/b] - soldiers hold their fire until they recognise you, waiting aimed where they are.[/*]
[*][b]Suppression[/b] - your bullets shake a soldier's aim for a second but never silence him: hit him and he fires back in a panic.[/*]
[*][b]Squads hunt where they last saw you[/b] for as long as you stay near it; only slipping away unseen loses them. A soldier keeps his rifle on the spot where you ducked out of sight, so peek from somewhere else.[/*]
[*][b]How soldiers see you[/b] - By day, in the open and in front of him, a soldier recognises you walking upright from 60 m, crouched and moving from 50 m and still from 40 m, and notices something from a little farther; movement in daylight catches his eye from 100 m, unless you stand in shade. At his side, crouched in high grass, or in shade by day, it is half. Cover hides you only where it hides your head, and tall grass on a crest between you hides you as a rock would, unless your head shows above it. At night he recognises you from 25 m at most, whatever you do, a quarter farther under a lamp, and in a sandstorm from 40 m at most. Behind him he never sees you, but hears you walk upright within 20 m; crouched, you can creep up unheard. Alerted soldiers see a quarter farther, and a soldier at the wheel only through his windscreen. The camo suit hides you crouched and still in high grass beyond 3 m. Beyond 30 m in front of him, or 20 m at his side, he needs a moment to notice you, longer the farther and the less visible you are, up to 4 seconds: running across open ground at 50 m gives you about 2, so a dash from cover to cover can go unseen.[/*]
[*][b]Weapons by range[/b] - pistols and SMGs lose accuracy with range. A shotgun is deadly out to 20 m and falls off fast past it.[/*]
[*][b]No rockets at you on foot[/b] - a soldier with an RPG or a Carl Gustav draws his other gun at you on foot, and keeps the launcher for you in a vehicle.[/*]
[*][b]Alerts end[/b] - a soldier who has lost you gives up after 90 seconds, walks back to where he was when the alert began and goes back to his post, where the game kept him searching for good.[/*]
[*][b]A combat log[/b] in bin\difficulty-overhaul-logs, one file per session and the last 20 kept: every hit on you and by you, and every shot at you with its chance. Attach it to a bug report.[/*]
[/list]
Everything is tuned on Hardcore. The difficulties differ only in how much you can take and how you heal; the soldiers are the same on every setting. Fights between soldiers, and between soldiers and your buddies, play as the game ships them.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/farcry2/mods/368]FCSE[/url] 1.4.0 or later, the plugin loader this runs in. Far Cry 2 1.03, Steam or GOG.[/*]
[*]JackAll 1.7.0 or the Vortex extension 0.6.0, or later. Older versions install the plugin but leave the soldiers' brain as it was, without saying so.[/*]
[/list]
[b][size=4]Installing[/size][/b]
The download is a JackAll layer, which both installers read as-is:
[list]
[*][b]Vortex[/b] - auto-installer handles the rest.[/*]
[*][b]JackAll[/b] - [url=https://jbebe.github.io/farcry-sdk/jackall/installing-mods/]here's a detailed instruction[/url] for JackAll installation.[/*]
[/list]
[b][size=4]Compatibility[/size][/b]
[list]
[*][b]Mods that change the soldiers' brain[/b] merge with it plan by plan, and a mod that replaces the brain whole still works: these changes go on top of it.[/*]
[*][b]Mods that change weapon damage or health[/b] change the numbers this mod multiplies.[/*]
[*][b]Mods that change bullet impacts or blood[/b] replace this mod's whole materialimpacts.xml, or it replaces theirs: whichever is installed last wins.[/*]
[*][b]Flashlight[/b] - its guards noticing your light does not work while this mod is installed.[/*]
[/list]
